    <item>
      <title>BP Can Solve Its Debt Problem Once and For All</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-10-15/bp-can-solve-its-debt-problem-once-and-for-all</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">090aece67385cc49d7d28919</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 04:00:35 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Fortune favors the bold — and the frugal. BP Plc decided in early February to suspend its $3 billion-a-year share buyback program. The move wasn’t popular with every shareholder, but it was necessary to preserve cash to pay down debt instead. Days later, the US and Israel attacked Iran, sending energy prices sharply higher. The ensuing windfall, plus the buyback savings, have created an unmissable opportunity: The British oil major can solve its balance-sheet problems once and for all.</description>
      <dc:creator>Javier Blas</dc:creator>
